<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Bail Application — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Section 480 & 483 BNSS 2023 / Section 437, 439 CrPC 1973 (Regular Bail) or Section 482 BNSS / 438 CrPC (Anticipatory Bail)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>Court Fee Stamp (₹10 - ₹20) + Vakalatnama Welfare Stamp</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Filed before Judicial Magistrate / Principal District & Sessions Court</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Affidavit of applicant's relative / surety to be attested before Oath Commissioner</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Sessions Court of the district where crime is registered</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>May be filed anytime after arrest or upon apprehension of arrest</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Copy of FIR and Complaint (FIR Form No. 1); Remand Application / Charge Sheet (if filed); Aadhaar Card and Local Solvency Proof of Surety; Medical Records (if bail sought on medical grounds)</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">BAIL APPLICATION</div>
<div class="draft-body">IN THE COURT OF THE PRINCIPAL DISTRICT AND SESSIONS JUDGE AT ________________________
CRL. MISC. NO. ___________ OF 2026
(IN CRIME NO. ________/2026 OF ________________________ POLICE STATION)

APPLICATION UNDER SECTION 483 OF BNSS 2023 (SECTION 439 CRPC) FOR GRANT OF REGULAR BAIL

PETITIONER / ACCUSED:
__________________________________________________, S/o __________________________________,
Aged _____ years, residing at ____________________________________________________________.
(Presently in Judicial Custody at Central Prison, ________________________)

                                    VERSUS

RESPONDENT:
STATE OF KARNATAKA,
Represented by Police Sub-Inspector, ________________________ Police Station.

GROUNDS FOR BAIL:
1. Petitioner is innocent, falsely implicated, and has clean antecedents.
2. Major part of investigation is completed; custody no longer required.
3. Petitioner is permanent resident with deep roots in society, no flight risk.
4. Petitioner undertakes to cooperate with investigation and not tamper with witnesses.
5. Ready to furnish solvent local surety to the satisfaction of the Hon'ble Court.

PRAYER:
Wherefore, Petitioner respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to release the Petitioner on regular bail in Crime No. ________/2026.

ADVOCATE FOR PETITIONER: _______________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>